Resolving WSL2 Deployment Error with Docker Desktop

The error occurs when deploying WSL2 distributions, specifically while checking the bootstrap version of the main distribution. This issue often arises due to misconfigurations in WSL or Docker Desktop.

Example

c:\windows\system32\wsl.exe -d docker-desktop -e cat /etc/wsl_bootstrap_version
exit status 0xffffffff
Steps to Resolve

Unregister and Restart Docker Desktop: If the docker-desktop distribution is corrupted, unregister it and restart Docker Desktop.

wsl --unregister docker-desktop
Update WSL: Ensure you are using the latest version of WSL.

wsl --update
Enable Required Features: Verify that both the Windows Subsystem for Linux and Virtual Machine Platform features are enabled.

dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux /all /norestart
dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart
Check Networking Configuration: If networking issues persist, modify .wslconfig to disable networking mode for Docker. Add the following to C:\Users\<YourUser>\.wslconfig:

[wsl2]
networkingMode=None
Verify File Permissions: Ensure that the vhdx file used by Docker is writable and accessible. If restored from a backup, remove any read-only flags.

Reinstall Docker Desktop: If none of the above steps work, reinstall Docker Desktop and ensure it is configured for WSL2.

By following these steps, you can resolve the deployment error and ensure smooth operation of WSL2 with Docker Desktop.

